WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.327 --> 00:00:20.571
When Ally arrived at Sandville Print Shop, Mateo was waiting outside for her.

2
00:00:21.212 --> 00:00:23.233
A bell jangled as they entered the shop.

3
00:00:24.474 --> 00:00:30.780
To their surprise, Coach Cross was standing behind the counter, wearing a T-shirt that read Your Message Here.

4
00:00:32.548 --> 00:00:32.888
"Hi, Coach.

5
00:00:34.169 --> 00:00:37.191
I thought you said your brother owns this shop," Ally said.

6
00:00:37.852 --> 00:00:38.592
The man laughed.

7
00:00:39.633 --> 00:00:43.976
"People always mix up my brother and me!

8
00:00:43.996 --> 00:00:46.658
I'm Eli, Coach Cross' brother.

9
00:00:47.699 --> 00:00:49.220
You must be Ally and Mateo.

10
00:00:50.881 --> 00:00:51.882
I'll be right with you kids.

11
00:00:52.542 --> 00:00:54.724
I just have to make some copies for another customer."

12
00:00:57.326 --> 00:01:00.208
Eli started up one of the shop's large copy machines.

13
00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:03.981
The machine was so loud, Ally could hardly hear her own thoughts.

14
00:01:05.221 --> 00:01:06.642
Eli came back to the counter.

15
00:01:06.662 --> 00:01:09.562
"I'm happy to help with your fundraiser.

16
00:01:10.063 --> 00:01:14.904
If you pay for the T-shirts and supply the design, I'll donate the cost of printing the shirts."

17
00:01:15.464 --> 00:01:18.745
"That's very generous of you," Mateo said loudly.

18
00:01:18.765 --> 00:01:21.106
"How much are the T-shirts?"

19
00:01:21.126 --> 00:01:26.347
"Five dollars each if you order between twenty and fifty shirts."

20
00:01:27.027 --> 00:01:32.194
Eli started to punch numbers into his calculator, but Ally already had the math figured out.

21
00:01:32.214 --> 00:01:40.060
"So, if we print fifty T-shirts, and charge fifteen dollars per shirt, we'll make over seven hundred dollars,"

22
00:01:40.521 --> 00:01:40.901
she said.

23
00:01:40.921 --> 00:01:46.625
"Minus the $250 you'll have to pay now to buy the T-shirts," Eli reminded her.

24
00:01:46.645 --> 00:01:50.589
"But we don't have $250."

25
00:01:52.190 --> 00:01:53.011
Mateo sighed.

26
00:01:54.512 --> 00:01:55.713
Ally pulled out her purse.

27
00:01:55.733 --> 00:01:57.374
"Yes, we do!

28
00:01:57.794 --> 00:01:59.336
I have a lot of money saved."

29
00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:02.522
"Great, I'll start the paperwork," Eli said.

30
00:02:04.664 --> 00:02:06.165
Mateo pulled Ally aside.

31
00:02:06.185 --> 00:02:08.847
"I can't ask you to pay for this, Ally."

32
00:02:08.867 --> 00:02:11.630
"But you're not asking me to pay, Mateo.

33
00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:12.851
I'm offering.

34
00:02:13.471 --> 00:02:18.455
Besides, I might as well spend my Earth money now, since it will do me no good once

35
00:02:18.515 --> 00:02:20.137
I head back to space with Lainie."

36
00:02:21.298 --> 00:02:22.118
Mateo grinned.

37
00:02:22.138 --> 00:02:24.020
"I didn't think of that!

38
00:02:24.861 --> 00:02:25.621
Thanks a lot.

39
00:02:26.002 --> 00:02:28.564
It's very nice of you to put the money down for us."

40
00:02:29.572 --> 00:02:30.393
"No problem!"

41
00:02:37.198 --> 00:02:38.680
Ally set the bills on the floor.

42
00:02:39.701 --> 00:02:42.503
Eli and Mateo looked at each other, confused.

43
00:02:42.523 --> 00:02:46.106
"Um, Ally, what are you doing?"

44
00:02:46.466 --> 00:02:47.207
Mateo asked.

45
00:02:47.227 --> 00:02:51.350
"You said to put the money down, so I did."

46
00:02:53.692 --> 00:02:56.174
Eli and Mateo laughed.

47
00:02:56.194 --> 00:02:58.316
"What's so funny?"

48
00:02:58.728 --> 00:02:59.308
Ally asked.

49
00:02:59.328 --> 00:03:04.210
"Putting money down is just an expression," Mateo said.

50
00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:06.550
"It means to pay for something."

51
00:03:07.811 --> 00:03:08.971
"Oh! I get it."

52
00:03:10.351 --> 00:03:13.492
Ally laughed as she picked the money up and handed it to Eli.

53
00:03:13.512 --> 00:03:15.873
"Great," he said.

54
00:03:15.893 --> 00:03:18.253
"Send me your design as soon as you can.

55
00:03:18.573 --> 00:03:20.794
I need only a day or two to print the shirts."

56
00:03:20.814 --> 00:03:23.135
"Thanks so much, Eli!"

57
00:03:23.695 --> 00:03:27.516
Mateo and Ally turned to leave when a dark-haired woman entered the shop.

58
00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:29.802
Her arms were full of blueprints.

59
00:03:30.822 --> 00:03:33.304
"Hello, Mateo," the woman said.

60
00:03:33.324 --> 00:03:35.526
"It's so nice to see you."

61
00:03:35.546 --> 00:03:38.829
"Hello, Mayor Clark," Mateo said.

62
00:03:38.849 --> 00:03:43.973
"You must be Ally," the mayor said.

63
00:03:43.993 --> 00:03:49.698
"I've eaten at Ray's Diner many times, but you're always so busy, I've never had the chance to

64
00:03:49.718 --> 00:03:50.138
meet you.

65
00:03:50.979 --> 00:03:53.401
I just love all you've done for the diner."

66
00:03:53.421 --> 00:03:56.944
"That's very nice of you to say," Ally said.

67
00:03:57.864 --> 00:04:03.870
"That Gourmet Greta review brought a lot of positive attention to the town, and so many new tourists.

68
00:04:04.671 --> 00:04:08.354
And now Lainie Polk's launch is set to bring even more people here!

69
00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:15.681
In many ways, the plans in these blueprints are happening thanks to you, Ally."

70
00:04:16.642 --> 00:04:17.844
Ally grinned proudly.

71
00:04:17.864 --> 00:04:22.008
"Just wait until my parents hear about this," she thought.

72
00:04:22.444 --> 00:04:27.367
"They will be so impressed to hear that even the mayor was thankful for all I did on

73
00:04:27.447 --> 00:04:31.529
Earth!" "Madam Mayor, what are the plans for?"

74
00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:32.690
Mateo asked.

75
00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:34.551
Just then his phone rang.

76
00:04:34.571 --> 00:04:40.795
"Oh, excuse me for a moment, this is my friend Bethany on the phone."

77
00:04:40.815 --> 00:04:42.796
"Of course."

78
00:04:44.617 --> 00:04:49.700
Mayor Clark set her blueprints on the counter and started talking to Eli about making copies of them.

79
00:04:50.464 --> 00:04:55.626
Between Mateo's talking on the phone and the noise of the copy machines, Ally wasn't sure she heard

80
00:04:55.706 --> 00:04:59.128
right. But she thought she heard the mayor say "soccer field."

81
00:05:00.528 --> 00:05:04.250
She tried to read the mayor's mind, but the shop was still too noisy.

82
00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:07.711
"I must have misheard her," Ally thought.

83
00:05:07.731 --> 00:05:13.393
"Why would an important person like the mayor of Sandville be thinking about a kids' soccer field?"

84
00:05:14.274 --> 00:05:15.954
Mateo disconnected his call.

85
00:05:15.974 --> 00:05:20.176
"Hey, Ally, Bethany and Kate want us to meet them at the park.

86
00:05:20.856 --> 00:05:24.062
They have a design for the T-shirt, and a big surprise!"

87
00:05:24.082 --> 00:05:26.266
"Sounds great!"

88
00:05:26.647 --> 00:05:27.168
Ally said.

89
00:05:27.188 --> 00:05:28.791
"Let's go!"
